*                       CORRECTION NUMBER 1 FOR BE FAP (SDA 1033)               
*                                                                               
*                                                                               
*              PREVENT NEW NUMBERING OF DECKS AT ASSEMBLY TIME.                 
*                  DELETE BF000010, BF100010, BF200010, BF300010                
*                                                                               
*              PROVIDE A CALLING SEQUENCE FOR FAP WHICH ALLOWS TAPE             
*              ASSIGNMENT AT EXECUTION TIME. TAPE ASSIGNMENT MAY BE BY          
*              UNITS ONLY..CHANNELS MAY NOT BE CHANGED.                         
*                  CHANGE BF004430-BF004440, CHANGE BF004730, INSERT            
*                  BF004731, CHANGE BF005040, CHANGE BF005260, INSERT           
*                  BF100151-BF100159, CHANGE BF100160, INSERT BF100161-         
*                  BF100169, CHANGE BF100170, INSERT BF100171-BF100179,         
*                  CHANGE BF020930, CHANGE BF103630, CHANGE BF206590            
*              THE INSERTION OF THE REMARK CARDS IS OPTIONAL. THEY ARE          
*              INCLUDED AS A DESCRIPTION OF THE CALL CONVENTIONS AND            
*              FOR CLARITY ON THE LISTING.                                      
*                                                                       BF004000
*              CALLING SEQUENCE FOR THE FAP MONITOR. IT IS NOW GIVEN BY BF004000
*                    BE SYS 3. THIS CALLING SEQUENCE AS USED BY THE     BF004000
*                    FAP MONITOR PROVIDES THE NECESSARY COMMUNICATION   BF004000
*                    BETWEEN BE FAP AND THE SYSTEM MONITOR.             BF004000
*              THE RETURNS ARE ALL FOR CONDITIONS OCCURRING AFTER THE   BF004000
*                    ASSEMBLY PROCESS HAS BEEN COMPLETED.               BF004000
*                                                                       BF004000
*                       TSX  100,4                                      BF004000
*                            EOF                                        BF004000
*                            ERR                                        BF004000
*                            NORMAL RETURN                              BF004000
*                            TAPES                                      BF004000
*                                                                       BF004000
*              EOF=RETURN TO BE TAKEN FOR AN INPUT END OF FILE ON SYSPITBF004000
*              ERR=RETURN TO BE TAKEN FOR INPUT READING ERROR ON SYSPIT BF004000
*              NORMAL RETURN=RETURN TO BE TAKEN IF A CONTROL CARD IS    BF004000
*                    FOUND ON SYSPIT.                                   BF004000
*              TAPES=A BSS TABLE OF TAPE ASSIGNMENTS TO BE FED DOWN     BF004000
*                    INTO THE FAP PROPER CALLING SEQUENCE.SEE FAP       BF004000
*                    CALLING SEQUENCE DESCRIPTION FOR DETAILS OF TABLE. BF004000
*                                                                       BF004000
*                                                                       BF004000
*              CALLING SEQUENCE FOR FAP PROPER.  THIS CALLING SEQUENCE  BF004000
*                    OCCURS IN THE FAP MONITOR AND ALL RETURNS ARE TO   BF004000
*                    THE FAP MONITOR. THE FAP MONITOR THEN, ACCORDING   BF004000
*                    TO THE RETURN, PERFORMS THE NECESSARY CLEAN-UP     BF004000
*                    OPERATIONS AND DETERMINES HOW CONTROL SHALL BE     BF004000
*                    RETURNED TO BE SYS 3.                              BF004000
*                       TSX  START,4                                    BF004000
*                            TAPES                                      BF004000
*                            ERROR                                      BF004000
*                            NORMAL RETURN                              BF004000
*              TAPES=A BSS TABLE OF THE FOLLOWING FORMAT AND ORDER.     BF004000
*                       TXL  SYSPIT    (TAPES)                          BF004000
*                  OR   PZE  SYSPIT    (TAPES)                          BF004000
*                       PZE  SYSPOT    (TAPES+1)                        BF004000
*                       PZE  BATCH     (TAPES+2)                        BF004000
*                       PZE  COLTAP    (TAPES+3)                        BF004000
*                    TXL PREFIX ON TAPES MEANS NO ON-LINE READING OPTIONBF004000
*                    PZE MEANS READ ON-LINE IF SENSE SWITCH 5 IS DOWN   BF004000
*              ERROR=RETURN TO BE TAKEN IN CASE OF FATAL ERROR OR       BF004000
*                    PROGRAMMER REQUEST FOR ONE PASS EDIT (IE EDIT,STOP)BF004000
*              NORMAL RETURN=RETURN TO FAP MONITOR FOR TRANSFERENCE OF  BF004000
*                    BINARY OUTPUT FROM B10 TO B4 AND EXAMINATION OF    BF004000
*                    NEXT CARD ON SYSPIT. (THIS SHOULD BE ONE OF THE    BF004000
*                    BE SYS CONTROL CARDS.)                             BF004000
       CAL     4,4                                                   3/9BF004430
       SLW     GOFAP+1                                               3/9BF004440
 GOFAP TSX     START,4             GO TO PASS 1 OF FAP PROPER        3/9BF004730
       PZE     **                  ADDRESS SUPPLIED BY CALLER        3/9BF004731
       SWT     5                   IS THIS ON-LINE INPUT             3/9BF005040
RDTAPE RTDA    X                                                     3/9BF005260
       CLA     1,4                                                   3/9BF100151
       STA     *+2                                                   3/9BF100152
       AXT     0,1                                                   3/9BF100153
 CLAT  CLA     **,1                                                  3/9BF100154
       STA     BSRAX               MODIFY NECESSARY                  3/9BF100155
       STA     RTDAX               TAPE REFERENCES                   3/9BF100156
       TPL     *+3                                                   3/9BF100157
       CLA     NOP                                                   3/9BF100158
       STO     SWT5                                                  3/9BF100159
       TXI     *+1,1,-1                                              3/9BF100160
       XEC     CLAT                PICK UP SYSPOT                    3/9BF100161
       STA     BSRAZ                                                 3/9BF100162
       STA     WTDAZ                                                 3/9BF100163
       TXI     *+1,1,-1                                              3/9BF100164
       XEC     CLAT                PICK UP BATCH                     3/9BF100165
       ORA     PLUS                                                  3/9BF100166
       STA     BSRBW                                                 3/9BF100167
       STA     WTBBW                                                 3/9BF100168
       STA     WEFBW                                                 3/9BF100169
       TXI     *+1,1,-1                                              3/9BF100170
       XEC     CLAT                PICK UP COLTAP                    3/9BF100171
       ORA     PLUS                                                  3/9BF100172
       STA     BSRBY                                                 3/9BF100173
       STA     RTBBY                                                 3/9BF100174
       STA     WTBBY                                                 3/9BF100175
       STA     WEFBY                                                 3/9BF100176
       STA     REWBY                                                 3/9BF100177
       AXT     VECTOR-FATOP,4      ZERO NECESSARY                    3/9BF100178
       STZ     VECTOR,4            CORES AND BUFFERS                 3/9BF100179
       TRA     2,4                 RETURN TO PICK UP NEXT CTRL CRD.  3/9BF020930
       TRA     2,4                 RETURN TO PICK UP NEXT CTRL CRD.  3/9BF103630
       TRA     3,4                 NORMAL RETURN TO MONITOR          3/9BF206590
